winemac.drv: Add a macdrv_functions table for Direct3D-on-Metal layers.

Translation layers such as DXMT (MIT) present through a CAMetalLayer that
they obtain from the Mac driver. They look up a `macdrv_functions` table
with dlsym() and expect a window data layout that upstream Wine no longer
has: a window only gets a client view once a client surface exists, and
the driver hides that view again whenever the GDI window surface is
flushed, expecting the next client_surface_present() to show it.

This adds the table, exported from winemac.so. It creates a client
surface on demand, keeps its view in sync from WindowPosChanged, leaves
it visible while its Metal view exists, and releases it with the Metal
view or the window.

Against wine-11.21. Tested with DXMT v0.80 on macOS 27.2 (Apple M5,
Rosetta 2): a Direct3D 11 test program and Audacity 4.0.2 (Qt 6).

